    // ── The city ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    // [ICON-CITY] Forged from isometric SVG sources, and every one of them went
    // through the same four steps the ICON-LIB header describes: flatten, merge by
    // colour, assign a tone tier, drop what is invisible at the size the map draws.
    //
    // THREE THINGS ARE WORTH KNOWING BEFORE ADDING MORE OF THESE.
    //
    // NOTHING IS CULLED AND THE SOURCE BOX IS KEPT. THIS IS A CORRECTION, and it is
    // the one lesson on this whole path worth carrying: the first cut of these icons
    // dropped every shape under 0.12% of the box and re-boxed 512 to 128 integers, on
    // the reasoning that a window mullion is invisible at 14px and costs a third of the
    // bytes. Both halves were true and the conclusion was still wrong -- what got
    // dropped WAS the icon. A church without its windows is a shed with a spire, and
    // the picker, the entity hero and a zoomed-in map all draw these far larger than
    // 14px. Integer coordinates on the source box are a third of a pixel at any size
    // this renders, so rounding is free. Culling was not. DO NOT RE-ADD IT.
    //
    // BYTES ARE NOT THE CONSTRAINT AND WERE NEVER MEASURED TO BE. 85 KB of path data
    // across thirteen icons is 3% of this file, and the map draws ONE icon per visible
    // node -- the cost that would matter is path COUNT per frame, which is 5-8 here
    // against castle1's 6. If that ever does bite, the answer is a reduced variant
    // chosen by draw size, not a permanently degraded descriptor.
    //
    // ONE PATH PER SOURCE COLOUR. Two colours merge only when they land on the same
    // slot, because then they render identically anyway.
    //
    // THE ACCENT RAMP IS RESERVED AND STRUCTURE IS NOT ALLOWED INTO IT. A found icon's
    // saturated colours are the parts that MEAN something -- a lit window, an awning, a
    // cross. They get a0-a3 so a theme can drive them separately from the masonry,
    // which is what makes a holographic map possible at all (see THEME-SLOT).
